<title>USA: Arco may purchase shares for benefit plan.</title>
<headline>Arco may purchase shares for benefit plan.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Atlantic Richfield Co on Tuesday said it may purchase up to $150 million worth of ARCO common stock on the open market to provide for current and future obligations under its 1985 Executive Long Term Incentive Plan (LTIP).</p>
<p>Last year, the company bought a total of 480,000 shares of common stock to satisfy obligations in connection with stock option exercises under the LTIP and conversion of the $3.00 and $2.80 preference stocks.</p>
</text>
